/*!
\page page_stssthit StSstHit

\ref StSstHit represents a single reconstructed space-point hit in the STAR Silicon Strip
Tracker (SST), the HFT-era upgrade replacement for the SSD.  The SST retains the same
double-sided strip geometry as the SSD but adds a third local-coordinate component and explicit
per-side ADC values.

\see StSstHitCollection

\section sec_ssthit_hierarchy Class Hierarchy

\verbatim
StObject
└── StMeasuredPoint
    └── StHit
        └── StSstHit
\endverbatim

Hits are collected in \ref StSstHitCollection.

\section sec_ssthit_members Data Members

\subsection subsec_ssthit_inherited Inherited from StHit

- <tt>UInt_t mHardwarePosition</tt> — Packed hardware word, identical bit layout to
  \ref StSsdHit: bits 4–12 = flat wafer index; bits 13–22 = N-side central strip; bits 23–27 =
  P-side offset; bits 28–29 = N-side cluster size − 1; bits 30–31 = P-side cluster size − 1.
- <tt>StThreeVectorF mPositionError</tt> — 1-σ errors (cm). <em>Not persisted.</em>
- <tt>Float_t mCharge</tt> — Cluster charge (ADC counts).
- <tt>Int_t mId</tt> — Cluster identifier.
- <tt>Int_t mIdTruth</tt> — Geant track ID (simulation only).
- <tt>UShort_t mQuality</tt> — Charge fraction from <tt>mIdTruth</tt> (percent).
- <tt>UChar_t mFitFlag</tt> — Non-zero if used in a track fit.
- <tt>UChar_t mTrackRefCount</tt> — Number of tracks referencing this hit.
- <tt>UShort_t mFlag</tt> — Hit status flag bitmask.

\subsection subsec_ssthit_own Own Data Members

- <tt>Float_t mLocalPosition[3]</tt> — Local hit position (cm): [0] = P-side strip direction,
  [1] = N-side strip direction, [2] = z (beam-axis component).
- <tt>UShort_t mADC[2]</tt> — ADC values: [0] = P-side cluster, [1] = N-side cluster.
- <tt>static StMemoryPool mPool</tt> — Per-class memory pool. <em>Not persisted.</em>

\section sec_ssthit_geometry Geometry

Identical sector/ladder/wafer layout to \ref StSsdHit: 20 ladders (1–20), 16 wafers per ladder
(1–16), four sectors.
<b>volumeID</b> = <tt>10000 × sector + 7000 + 100 × wafer + ladder</tt>.

\section sec_ssthit_methods Key Methods

- <tt>unsigned int ladder() const</tt> — Ladder number (1–20).
- <tt>unsigned int wafer() const</tt> — Wafer number (1–16).
- <tt>unsigned int sector() const</tt> — Sector (1–4).
- <tt>unsigned int centralStripNSide() const</tt> — N-side central strip index.
- <tt>unsigned int centralStripPSide() const</tt> — P-side central strip index.
- <tt>unsigned int clusterSizeNSide() const</tt> — N-side cluster size.
- <tt>unsigned int clusterSizePSide() const</tt> — P-side cluster size.
- <tt>float localPosition(unsigned int i) const</tt> — Local coordinate along axis <tt>i</tt> (0–2, cm).
- <tt>void setLocalPosition(float u, float v, float w)</tt> — Set P-side, N-side, and z (cm).
- <tt>void setADC(unsigned short adcP, unsigned short adcN)</tt> — Set P-side and N-side ADC.
- <tt>int getADC(unsigned int i) const</tt> — ADC for side <tt>i</tt> (0 = P-side, 1 = N-side).
- <tt>virtual int volumeID() const</tt> — Packed geometry ID.
- <tt>StDetectorId detector() const</tt> — Returns <tt>kSstId</tt>.

\section sec_ssthit_ownership Object Ownership

\ref StSstHit uses a custom <tt>StMemoryPool</tt> allocator.  Ownership transfers to the
framework on insertion.
\warning Do <b>not</b> <tt>delete</tt> \ref StSstHit pointers obtained from the collection.

\section sec_ssthit_usage Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
StSstHitCollection* sstColl = event->sstHitCollection();
if (!sstColl) return;

for (unsigned int iLadder = 0; iLadder < sstColl->numberOfLadders(); ++iLadder) {
    const StSstLadderHitCollection* ladder = sstColl->ladder(iLadder);
    if (!ladder) continue;
    for (unsigned int iWafer = 0; iWafer < ladder->numberOfWafers(); ++iWafer) {
        const StSstWaferHitCollection* wafer = ladder->wafer(iWafer);
        if (!wafer) continue;
        const StSPtrVecSstHit& hits = wafer->hits();
        for (const StSstHit* hit : hits) {
            float localP = hit->localPosition(0); // P-side (cm)
            float localN = hit->localPosition(1); // N-side (cm)
            int adcP = hit->getADC(0);
            int adcN = hit->getADC(1);
        }
    }
}
\endcode

*/
